.TH SSHX 1 "2026-11-17" "sshx" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sshx \- a secure web-based, collaborative terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshx
.RB [ \-\-server\ \fIURL\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-shell\ \fICOMMAND\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-name\ \fINAME\fR ]
.RB [ \-\-enable\-readers ]
.RB [ \-\-quiet ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sshx
starts a local shell in a pseudoterminal and shares it through a web-based
collaborative terminal session. It connects to a remote sshx server, prints a
URL for the session, and streams terminal input and output end\-to\-end
encrypted over WebSocket connections.
.PP
Anyone with the writable link can type into the shared terminal, and anyone
with the read\-only link can watch it in real time. The terminal state is
encrypted with Argon2 and AES, so the sshx server cannot read session data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-server\ \fIURL\fR
Address of the remote sshx server (defaults to
.I https://sshx.io ,
or the
.B SSHX_SERVER
environment variable).
.TP
.BR \-\-shell\ \fICOMMAND\fR
Local shell command to run in the terminal. Defaults to the user's default
shell.
.TP
.BR \-\-name\ \fINAME\fR
Session name displayed in the title. Defaults to
.IR user @ hostname .
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-readers
Enable read\-only access mode, generating separate URLs for viewers and
editors.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Quiet mode, only prints the session URL to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Print version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B sshx
exits with status 0 on a clean shutdown after Ctrl\-C, and non\-zero if the
session fails to start or the connection is lost.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Share your default shell:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sshx
.fi
.RE
.PP
Share a specific command read\-only:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sshx \-\-shell "htop" \-\-enable\-readers
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sshx\-server (1)
.PP
https://sshx.io
